# ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample Design

Date: 2026-06-27

Status: Implemented first pass on 2026-06-27.

Scope: editor-only, sample-only Animation Blueprint ControlRig AnimGraph node
authoring. Runtime/gameplay code and original asset mutation are out of scope.

## Purpose

`ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample` is a narrow UnrealMCP
bridge command for requests that need a safe sample AnimBP with a ControlRig
AnimGraph node when the source graph does not already contain one.

The command should:

- duplicate or reuse a target sample AnimBP under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or
  `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`;
- insert one `UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig` in a small, predictable sample chain;
- bind the requested ControlRig class or ControlRig Blueprint generated class;
- optionally expose bounded input pins and set simple default values;
- compile, optionally save, and read back topology/settings evidence.

The command exists to avoid failed attempts to treat direct transient ControlRig
proof or Python pin-array edits as a complete compiled AnimBP node insertion.

## Ieta Review

Request class: add a ControlRig AnimGraph node to a safe sample AnimBP for
proof, study, or follow-on forced-driver testing.

Existing routes checked:

- `controlrig_direct_gate_probe` proves a transient ControlRig class can respond
  to properties or curves.
- `sample_controlrig_pre_post_runtime_pose` proves direct transient rig
  hierarchy deltas.
- `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` exposes and sets defaults on an
  existing ControlRig AnimGraph node.
- `ensure_controlrig_forced_driver_animbp` inserts or reuses a sample driver
  before an existing ControlRig node.
- `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology` can confirm whether the graph already
  contains a ControlRig node.

Why existing routes are insufficient: they do not safely create a new
`UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig`, link it into an AnimGraph, and bind a ControlRig
class in a compiled sample AnimBP.

Asset mutation boundary: source AnimBP and source ControlRig assets are
read-only. The command may modify only the target sample AnimBP under
`/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`.

Implemented command: `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`.

Default safety guard: require a source AnimBP and a target sample path, reject
target paths outside sample/temp roots, reject mutation of the source AnimBP,
and return `unsupported_feature` for arbitrary original graph rewrites.

Approval status: user approved Ieta/Tivret continuation on 2026-06-27. First
implementation remains editor-only, sample-only, and runtime-code-free.

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

Use installed UE 5.6 headers as local truth:

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ControlRig editor AnimGraph node | `Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRigDeveloper/Public/AnimGraphNode_ControlRig.h` | Use `UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig` with its `FAnimNode_ControlRig Node` member rather than generic Python property guesses. |
| Runtime ControlRig node | `Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRig/Public/AnimNode_ControlRig.h` | Bind with `FAnimNode_ControlRig::SetControlRigClass()` or equivalent safe C++ path. |
| ControlRig custom-property base | `Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRig/Public/AnimNode_ControlRigBase.h` | Respect custom property and exposed pin synchronization. |
| ControlRig input/output mapping | `Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRigDeveloper/Public/ControlRigIOMapping.h` | Rebuild or expose pins through node/editor APIs, not by mutating optional-pin arrays alone. |
| ControlRig asset class | `Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRigDeveloper/Public/ControlRigBlueprint.h` | Resolve a `UControlRigBlueprint` to `GetControlRigClass()` when a rig asset path is supplied. |
| AnimGraph node base | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_Base.h` | Treat node placement and pose links as editor graph work. |
| Animation graph schema | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimationGraphSchema.h` | Use schema-compatible graph connections and reconstruction. |
| Blueprint mutation and compile | `Kismet2/BlueprintEditorUtils.h`, `Kismet2/KismetEditorUtilities.h` | Mark structurally modified, compile, then inspect/read back. |

## Command Schema

Proposed input fields:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `source_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Existing AnimBP to duplicate or use as the template. |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Must be under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`. |
| `control_rig_asset_path` | string | optional | ControlRig Blueprint asset path. Never mutated. |
| `control_rig_class_path` | string | optional | Generated class or native concrete ControlRig class path. Required if asset path is absent. Reject abstract base classes such as `/Script/ControlRig.ControlRig` before instantiation. |
| `insert_mode` | enum | `input_pose_to_controlrig_to_root` | MVP should support only a minimal chain that routes input pose through ControlRig to output. |
| `input_defaults` | object | `{}` | Bounded simple defaults for exposed ControlRig inputs. |
| `expose_input_pins` | array[string] | `[]` | Optional explicit input names. Reject unknown or unsupported property types. |
| `allow_existing_target_reuse` | bool | `true` | Reuse target when it already exists and is under sample/temp root. |
| `replace_existing_sample_graph` | bool | `false` | If true, replace only the target sample graph chain. |
| `compile` | bool | `true` | Compile after mutation. |
| `save_asset` | bool | `false` | Save only the target sample asset. |
| `dry_run` | bool | `false` | Resolve assets and planned actions without mutation. |

MVP `insert_mode` should stay narrow. Do not support arbitrary insertion before
or after any user-selected node until a concrete request justifies the extra
graph safety surface.

First implementation note: v1 implements only
`input_pose_to_controlrig_to_root`. It resolves the ControlRig class, creates or
reuses the target sample AnimBP, adds/reuses a Linked Input Pose and
`UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig`, connects pose links, compiles, optionally saves,
and returns topology readback. It does not apply `input_defaults` or
`expose_input_pins` directly; use `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults`
after the node exists.

## Response Schema

Return structured evidence:

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `success` | Whether the sample command completed. |
| `dry_run` | Whether mutation was skipped. |
| `source_anim_bp_path` | Source asset path. |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | Target sample asset path. |
| `source_modified` | Must be false. |
| `target_modified` | True only when dry run is false and the target changed. |
| `control_rig_class` | Resolved `UControlRig` class path. |
| `created_node_id` | New or reused ControlRig editor node GUID. |
| `created_links` | Pose-link summary from input pose to ControlRig to output. |
| `exposed_inputs` | Inputs exposed or validated. |
| `input_defaults_applied` | Defaults applied with per-field status. |
| `compile_result` | Compile status, warnings, and errors. |
| `compile_succeeded` / `save_succeeded` | Final requested compile/save outcome. Top-level `success` must be false when a requested compile or save fails. |
| `completion_errors` | Failure tokens such as `compile_failed` or `save_failed` when finalization did not complete. |
| `partial_target_modified` | Present on error responses after target preparation. True means the sample target was created or partially edited before the failure and should be inspected or cleaned up before chaining more writes. |
| `readback` | Topology/settings summary from existing inspectors or equivalent C++ readback. |
| `warnings` | Bounded warnings for skipped inputs or unsupported graph shapes. |

## Guardrails

Forbidden patterns:

- modifying the source AnimBP or source ControlRig asset;
- writing outside `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`;
- adding a ControlRig node to an arbitrary original AnimBP by default;
- using direct transient ControlRig proof as compiled AnimBP proof;
- instantiating abstract `UControlRig` base classes or other non-concrete
  ControlRig classes;
- treating `show_pin_for_properties` edits alone as exposed-pin success;
- hand-editing graph node arrays, pin arrays, or generated class internals from
  Python;
- accepting unbounded input names, nested struct defaults, or object reference
  defaults in MVP.

Stop and return a structured error when the source graph has a topology that
cannot be safely reduced to the supported sample chain.

## Verification

Docs-only verification for this design:

- `git diff --check`
- Markdown link and trailing-whitespace sanity checks.

Implementation verification:

1. `dry_run=true` resolves source AnimBP, target path, and ControlRig class
   without dirtying any package.
2. Create a target sample AnimBP and compile.
3. Read back topology with `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology` and confirm
   the ControlRig node class, pose links, and output link.
4. Read back settings with `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings`.
5. If input defaults were requested, run or reuse
   `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` style readback.
6. If a live target exists, prove compiled graph behavior with
   `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose(mode=pose_watch_capture)`.
7. Confirm the source AnimBP and ControlRig asset were not marked dirty.
8. Negative fixture: `control_rig_class_path=/Script/ControlRig.ControlRig`
   must return a structured error without an ensure, crash, target mutation, or
   dirty package.

